319	## DAG traversal
320	
321	`DagTraversal` and `AsyncDagTraversal` traverse a discovered acyclic graph in two lifecycle orders: `ON_WORK_READY` visits eligible initial work, and `ON_SUBGRAPH_READY` visits structural completion after the vertex’s work, discovery, and retained children complete. Under default `afterWorkReadyChain`, normal initial visitor-chain completion (including empty or filtered chains) satisfies work dependents; `externalSettlement` requires guarded host settlement; committed completion satisfies completion dependents. `dependsOnWork: [p]` waits for p's completed initial work (W); `dependsOnSubgraphCompletion: [p]` waits for p's committed `ON_SUBGRAPH_READY` transition (C), including closed discovery and completion of every retained child. Both lists gate `ON_WORK_READY` conjunctively. Completion admission or an unfinished async completion callback does not satisfy C. Dependencies do not create structural parent/child edges; graph sources have no implicit parent W by default. Set `dependsOnWorkDefault: 'discoveryParentWork'` to inherit parent W when `dependsOnWork` is omitted; explicit lists, including `[]`, always win. Tree sources retain structural order and parent dependencies and reject explicit `rootWorkDependencies` or `dependsOnWorkDefault` options, including configuration patches. Graph source defaults are `rootWorkDependencies: 'honor'` and `dependsOnWorkDefault: 'none'`.
